// Updating a nested field is compositional -- there is no special "deep
// update" syntax. Read the inner record off the base with a projection, update
// it with its own `#{ ... | ... }`, and hand that as the override for the outer
// field (proposal-value-semantics-mvp §3.1). Each layer is an ordinary update.
def outer = #{ tag = "t", inner = #{ x = 1, y = 2 } };

// `outer.inner` reads the inner record (a projection, delivering a computation
// that is sequenced for us); the inner update rebuilds it with y = 9; the outer
// update overlays the rebuilt inner. `outer` is untouched throughout.
#{ outer | inner = #{ outer.inner | y = 9 } }

// The harness checks:
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-last-value: #{inner = #{x = 1, y = 9}, tag = "t"}
